2. Can an interface have non-abstract methods?

   1. Yes, from Java 8 onwards, interfaces can have default and static methods.
   2. Default methods have an implementation and can be overridden by implementing classes.
   3. Static methods belong to the interface itself and are called using the interface name.
   4. From Java 9, interfaces can also have private methods to reuse common logic.

