7. What happens if an exception occurs during Stream execution?

   1. The exception is propagated to the caller when the operation is executed.
   2. The stream pipeline stops processing after an unhandled exception.
   3. We can handle exceptions using try-catch inside the lambda or handle them before passing data to the stream.
   4. Streams do not automatically retry failed operations.

