10. What happens if we don't provide a custom Executor and want to execute 100 tasks in parallel?

   1. CompletableFuture normally uses the common ForkJoinPool when we don't provide an Executor.
   2. It does not create 100 dedicated threads for 100 tasks.
   3. Tasks share the common thread pool, so they may execute concurrently or wait for available workers.
   4. For production applications, I prefer a custom thread pool to control concurrency and isolate workloads.

