11. What is eager and lazy dependency injection in Spring Boot?

   1. Eager initialisation means a bean is created during application startup.
   2. Lazy initialisation means a bean is created only when it is first required.
   3. By default, Spring singleton beans are eagerly initialised.
   4. We can use @Lazy on a bean or injection point to enable lazy initialisation.

   Example:

   @Lazy
   @Service
   public class ReportService {
   }

   To enable lazy initialisation globally:

   spring.main.lazy-initialization=true

