13. How do you handle exceptions in Spring Boot controllers?

   1. I use @RestControllerAdvice to handle exceptions globally.
   2. I use @ExceptionHandler to handle specific exception types.
   3. I return meaningful HTTP status codes and error messages.
   4. I also log exceptions with proper details for debugging without exposing internal information to clients.

   Example:

   @RestControllerAdvice
   public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

       @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
       public ResponseEntity<String> handleNotFound(
               ResourceNotFoundException ex) {

           return ResponseEntity
                   .status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
                   .body(ex.getMessage());
       }
   }

