19. A service takes a long time to respond. How will you handle it?

   1. I will configure connection timeouts and response timeouts so requests do not wait indefinitely.
   2. I will use retries with exponential backoff for temporary failures.
   3. I will implement a Circuit Breaker to stop repeated calls when the downstream service is unhealthy.
   4. I can also use asynchronous processing or fallback responses depending on business requirements.

   Important concepts:

   - Timeout: Stops waiting after a configured duration.
   - Retry: Tries the failed operation again.
   - Exponential Backoff: Increases the waiting time between retries.
   - Circuit Breaker: Temporarily stops calls to an unhealthy service.
   - Bulkhead: Isolates resources so one failure does not affect everything.

