21. How will you ensure at-least-once delivery semantics in Kafka?

   1. I will disable automatic offset commits and commit offsets only after successful processing.
   2. If processing fails, I will avoid committing the offset so Kafka can deliver the message again.
   3. I will implement idempotent processing using a unique event ID to prevent duplicate business updates.
   4. For failures, I will use retry handling and a Dead Letter Topic for messages that cannot be processed.

   Important: At-least-once delivery can produce duplicate messages, so consumer-side idempotency is essential.

