OVERALL RECOMMENDED DESIGN

1. Use constructor injection instead of field injection.
2. Use database locking and idempotency instead of the in-memory HashMap.
3. Keep inventory updates and order status updates within one database transaction.
4. Publish notifications through the Transactional Outbox pattern after successful commit.
5. Fetch inventory in batches to avoid N+1 queries.
6. Use global exception handling and proper logging.
